@startuml whole-project-composite-states

' Everything this project has as a state machine, in ONE self-contained
' diagram — no other file needed to read it. Every state and edge here is
' verified against the same sources as the individual diagrams it absorbs:
' App\Enums\OrderStatus, App\Enums\PaymentStatus,
' App\Actions\Order\TransitionOrderStatus, routes/web.php, canAccessPanel().
' Verified 2026-09-07. If this diagram and any of those disagree, the code
' is right — regenerate.

title The whole project as one state machine

skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor<<terminal>> #FFE0E0
  BackgroundColor<<paid>> #E0F5E0
  BackgroundColor<<fulfil>> #E8F0FF
  BackgroundColor<<money_in>> #E0F5E0
  BackgroundColor<<live>> #E8F0FF
}

state "IP allowed?" as IpGate <<choice>>
state "Blocked" as IpBlocked <<terminal>>
IpBlocked : host/firewall level — this app has\nNO general IP allowlist or blacklist of its\nown; if one exists it is infrastructure\nconfig outside this diagram's code, not a\ncondition any Action or middleware evaluates

state "Has a valid session cookie?" as SessionGate <<choice>>
SessionGate : checked once, at the first\nrequest of a visit — AuthenticateSession\n/ EnsureAccountIsActive re-check it on\nEVERY later request (see below)

[*] --> IpGate : any visit to the site
IpGate --> IpBlocked : no
IpGate --> SessionGate : yes\n(the overwhelmingly common case —\nthere is no real gate here today)
SessionGate --> Anon : no cookie,\nor cookie's session\nhas no authenticated user
SessionGate --> Customer : valid session,\nauthenticated user\n(re-verified by AuthenticateSession\n+ EnsureAccountIsActive on THIS\nand every later request, not\ntrusted from the cookie alone)

state "Stripe IP allowlisted?" as StripeIpGate <<choice>>
state "Rejected — not Stripe" as StripeIpBlocked <<terminal>>

[*] --> StripeIpGate : POST /stripe/webhook\n(external, independent of\nany visitor session above)
StripeIpGate --> StripeIpBlocked : no
StripeIpGate --> PPending : yes

state "Visitor journey" as Journey {

  state "Anonymous" as Anon {
    state "Browsing" as Browsing
    Browsing : /catalogue, /products/{slug}, /journal,\n/about, /contact, /faq, /delivery,\n/payment-information, /terms, /privacy, /cookies
    state "Shopping (cart)" as CartState
    CartState : /cart
    Browsing --> CartState : add to cart
    CartState --> Browsing : keep browsing
  }

  state "Authenticating" as AuthFlow {
    state "Login" as Login
    Login : /login (guest middleware)
    state "Register" as Register
    Register : /register (guest middleware)
  }

  state "Authenticated customer" as Customer {
    state "Browsing (signed in)" as CustBrowsing
    state "Shopping (signed in)" as CustCart
    state "Account" as Account
    Account : /account/password\n/account/orders\n(scoped to auth()->user()->orders())
    CustBrowsing --> CustCart : add to cart
    CustBrowsing --> Account : view account
    Account --> CustBrowsing : back
  }

  Anon --> AuthFlow : follow /login or /register
  AuthFlow --> Anon : back (still no session)
  AuthFlow --> Customer : credentials accepted
  Customer --> Anon : **POST /logout**\n(session invalidated,\ntoken regenerated,\nredirect to /catalogue)

  state "Staff (panel access)" as Staff <<paid>>
  Staff : /admin/* — canAccessPanel():\nrole membership (STAFF_ROLES)\nAND is_active, re-checked EVERY request
  state "Denied — 403" as PanelDenied <<terminal>>

  Customer --> Staff : has a STAFF_ROLES role\nand is_active
  Customer --> PanelDenied : visits /admin,\nno role or deactivated
  PanelDenied --> Customer : back to storefront

  state "Order tracking" as Tracking
  Tracking : /orders/track — order number\nAND email together, rate-limited\n(sequential numbers alone would\nenumerate every address)
  Anon --> Tracking : has order number + email
  Customer --> Tracking : also reachable while signed in
}

state "Checkout" as CheckoutSuper {
  CheckoutSuper : same CheckoutPage component whether\nguest (§37 #6) or signed in (§37 #7) —\nonly difference is prefilled details\nand whether order.user_id is set

  state "Order created" as OrderCreated <<paid>>
  OrderCreated : **ONE transaction:**\nCreateOrder (reserves stock,\nredeems coupon, snapshots VAT)\n+ RecordPayment

  [*] --> OrderCreated

  state "Payment" as PaymentSuper {
    PaymentSuper : §13, ADR-0004. Guards out-of-order Stripe\nwebhooks, NOT a user — UNIQUE on\npayment_events.stripe_event_id stops\none event applying twice (a different problem)

    state "Pending" as PPending <<live>>
    PPending : payment row exists,\nno money moved yet
    state "Processing" as PProcessing <<live>>
    PProcessing : intent confirmed,\nawaiting settlement
    state "Paid" as PPaid <<money_in>>
    PPaid : paid_at stamped;\nthe ONLY writer is the webhook
    state "Failed" as PFailed <<live>>
    PFailed : NOT terminal — Stripe allows retry\non the same PaymentIntent
    state "PartiallyRefunded" as PPartial <<money_in>>
    PPartial : refunded_amount < amount
    state "Disputed" as PDisputed
    PDisputed : chargeback opened\n(charge.dispute.created)
    state "Cancelled" as PCancelled <<terminal>>
    PCancelled : intent cancelled —\ncannot be revived
    state "Refunded" as PRefunded <<terminal>>
    PRefunded : full refund — end of the payment

    [*] --> PPending : RecordPayment (order placed)

    PPending --> PProcessing
    PPending --> PPaid : webhook arrives before\nany processing update
    PPending --> PFailed
    PPending --> PCancelled

    PProcessing --> PPaid : payment_intent.succeeded
    PProcessing --> PFailed : payment_intent.payment_failed
    PProcessing --> PCancelled

    PFailed --> PPending : retry
    PFailed --> PProcessing : retry
    PFailed --> PPaid : retry succeeds outright
    PFailed --> PCancelled

    PPaid --> PRefunded : full refund
    PPaid --> PPartial : partial refund
    PPaid --> PDisputed : chargeback

    PPartial --> PPartial : further partial refund\n(refunded_amount changes,\nstatus does not)
    PPartial --> PRefunded : topped up to full
    PPartial --> PDisputed

    PDisputed --> PPaid : merchant WINS
    PDisputed --> PRefunded : merchant LOSES

    PCancelled --> [*]
    PRefunded --> [*]

    note right of PFailed
      Failed loops back INTO the live
      region — not a dead end. Only
      Cancelled and Refunded are terminal.
    end note

    note bottom of PDisputed
      charge.dispute.created moves it IN.
      The closing events (charge.dispute.closed)
      are NOT handled yet — the move back out
      is currently a manual panel action.
    end note
  }

  OrderCreated --> PaymentSuper : CreateStripeIntent (card path)
  OrderCreated --> Confirmation : **cash on delivery**\n(no intent, no Stripe Elements —\nCreateStripeIntent refuses COD)

  state "Order confirmation page" as Confirmation
  Confirmation : /checkout/confirmation/{order}\n**NOT proof of payment** — the customer can\nclose the tab, lose connection, or never see\nthis page and the payment still completes,\nbecause the ONLY writer of payments.status\nis the webhook, on a completely different path

  PPaid --> Confirmation : redirect after confirmPayment()\n(the webhook path is separate\nand asynchronous — see above)
}

Customer --> CheckoutSuper : proceed to checkout
Anon --> CheckoutSuper : proceed to checkout (guest)
CheckoutSuper --> Journey : back to browsing

state "Order fulfilment" as OrderSuper {
  OrderSuper : §18, ADR-0004 (legality) + ADR-0011 (side effects\nlive on the transition, not a wrapper Action).\n**TransitionOrderStatus is the ONLY writer**\nof orders.status and order_status_histories.

  state "New" as ONew
  state "AwaitingPayment" as OAwaiting <<paid>>
  OAwaiting : Stripe orders only
  state "Paid" as OPaid <<paid>>
  state "Confirmed" as OConfirmed <<paid>>
  state "Preparing" as OPreparing <<fulfil>>
  state "ReadyForShipment" as OReady <<fulfil>>
  state "Shipped" as OShipped <<fulfil>>
  state "Delivered" as ODelivered <<fulfil>>
  state "Cancelled" as OCancelled
  state "Returned" as OReturned
  state "Refunded" as ORefunded <<terminal>>

  [*] --> ONew : CreateOrder\n(every order lands here,\nregardless of payment method)

  ONew --> OAwaiting : card payment
  ONew --> OConfirmed : **cash on delivery**\n(skips the payment leg entirely —\nroughly half of orders take this leg)
  ONew --> OCancelled : **ReleaseStock**

  OAwaiting --> OPaid : webhook confirms
  OAwaiting --> OCancelled : **ReleaseStock**

  OPaid --> OConfirmed
  OPaid --> OCancelled : **ReleaseStock**
  OPaid --> ORefunded

  OConfirmed --> OPreparing
  OConfirmed --> OCancelled : **ReleaseStock**
  OConfirmed --> ORefunded

  OPreparing --> OReady
  OPreparing --> OCancelled : **ReleaseStock**

  OReady --> OShipped : **CompleteSale**
  OReady --> OCancelled : **ReleaseStock**

  OShipped --> ODelivered
  OShipped --> OReturned : **RestockReturn**

  ODelivered --> OReturned : **RestockReturn**

  OCancelled --> ORefunded
  OReturned --> ORefunded

  ORefunded --> [*]

  note right of ONew
    Two entry legs: COD goes New --> Confirmed
    directly, never touching AwaitingPayment or
    Paid. This is entirely independent of which
    state the PAYMENT state machine above is in —
    the two enums do not reference each other.
  end note

  note as EffectsNote
    **Inventory effects live on the edge, not in a wrapper**
    (TransitionOrderStatus::applyInventoryEffect).
    Only three target statuses carry one:
    --> Cancelled   ReleaseStock    (frees the reservation)
    --> Shipped     CompleteSale    (reservation becomes a sale)
    --> Returned    RestockReturn   (stock comes back)
    Every other transition has no inventory effect. ADR-0011:
    a caller reaching Cancelled cannot skip releasing stock
    by forgetting a wrapper Action.
  end note

  note bottom of ORefunded
    The graph is acyclic — proven by
    tests/Unit/Enums/TransitionMatrixTest.php —
    which is what makes a repeated transition a
    safe no-op rather than a race.
  end note
}

Confirmation --> OrderSuper : order placed —\nOrderSuper begins independently\nof whatever PaymentSuper does next

note as WholeNote
  <b>Payment and Order are two SEPARATE state machines running on the same order concurrently, not one combined graph.</b>
  An order can sit in Confirmed while its payment sits in Disputed; neither enum
  references or knows the other's current state directly — the only
  connection between them is that the SAME order and payment row exist,
  and TransitionOrderStatus/TransitionPaymentStatus are each the sole
  writer of their own column.
end note

state "Visitor leaves" as SiteExit <<terminal>>
SiteExit : closes the tab, navigates away, or the\nsession simply expires — no server-side\nevent marks this; it is the visitor's own\nchoice, reachable from literally anywhere above

Journey --> SiteExit : close site
CheckoutSuper --> SiteExit : close site\n(mid-checkout abandonment —\nthe order row already exists;\nsee OrderSuper's own states\nfor what happens to it)
OrderSuper --> SiteExit : close site
IpBlocked --> SiteExit

note right of SiteExit
  Modeled once, at the top level, rather than
  repeating a "close site" edge on every leaf
  state inside Journey/CheckoutSuper/OrderSuper —
  a composite state's own exit transition covers
  every substate inside it in PlantUML's semantics,
  so one edge per top-level region is sufficient
  and equivalent to one per leaf.
end note

@enduml
